It looks like the problem is misaligned parentheses in the first return statement.  The return() closes after the log(sigma), leaving the "- (1 + inv_xi) * log(z1)" dangling.

I know the error message did not explain the error precisely and left a blank after the colon. On the other hand, it did point to the problematic piece of code.  We hope to find time for some major improvements in the compiler, including better error trapping.  If anyone on this list is interested in contributing to this effort, please let me know.

Many kinds of programming errors can be tracked down by running a nimbleFunction uncompiled, directly in R.  Unfortunately R is not bothered by the offending syntax in this case.

